c=json.loads((r/'tools/game-series.json').read_text());c['swarmsim']={'name':'Swarm Sim','symbol':'✦','revision':'swarmsim-v1','package':['game.html','data.js','core.js','render.js','game.js'],'category':'Insect colony idle strategy','summary':'20 producer tiers · 11 army tiers · energy abilities · ascension','controls':'Tap to hatch · quantity selector · keyboard sections','variants':[{'kicker':a,'title':b,'copy':t,'tone':'night'} for a,b,t in [('A LITTLE COLONY. A BIG WORLD.','From three drones to a hive mind.','Start with meat and larvae. Hatch queens, nests and twenty producer tiers while an original animated colony grows.'),('THE CLASSIC GROWTH LOOP','Sacrifice. Regrow. Multiply.','Queens consume drones and then make new drones. Plan purchases, build hatcheries, expand territory and buy twin upgrades.'),('ENERGY CHANGES THE PLAN','Rush. Clone. Warp. Ascend.','Five nexus, six energy abilities, eleven troop tiers and ten permanent mutations. Spend energy to lower the cost of the next world.'),('YOUR COLONY KEEPS GROWING','Close the tab. Come back stronger.','Analytic offline catch-up, readable huge numbers, purchase undo, backup import/export, touch-friendly controls and three native mods.')]],'features':[['Keep the producer chain growing','Twenty meat tiers, eleven military tiers, creature sacrifices, twin upgrades, hatcheries and expansions.'],['A new world remembers','Energy storage and generation creatures, six spells, cocoon storage, ascension and ten mutation categories.'],['An idle colony you can keep','Original insect artwork, analytic catch-up, keyboard and touch, clear purchase costs, backups and three isolated mods.']],'mods':[['swarmharvest','Double Harvest','✦','Drones gather twice as much meat. Producer sacrifices and prices stay the same.'],['swarmlarvae','Extra Hatchlings','◒','Double the real rate of passive larvae production.'],['swarmenergy','Charged Nexus','ϟ','Nexus generate energy five times faster; energy capacity and spell costs still apply.']]};(r/'tools/game-series.json').write_text(json.dumps(c,indent=2)+'\n')
(d/'README.md').write_text('# Swarm Sim\n\nOriginal PocketVM idle colony inspired by the classic browser Swarm Simulator. The production and purchase structure uses 20 meat producer tiers, 11 territory units, sacrifice costs, faster/twin upgrades, hatcheries, expansions, five nexus, six energy spells, cocoon storage, energy-specialist creatures, ten permanent mutations and ascension. Opening balance is 35 meat, 10 larvae and 1 larva/second. Original illustration, insect icons and interface; no source code or art copied from Swarm Simulator. Numeric balance reference: developer\'s published data at https://github.com/swarmsim/swarm and game at https://www.swarmsim.com/.\n\nBuy quantities 1, 10, 100, 25% affordable or Maximum. Costs show which lower-tier creatures will be sacrificed. Purchases can be undone for ten seconds while retaining elapsed production. Keyboard 1–6 selects sections, U undoes, Escape closes review. Large touch targets, responsive layouts, number notation and still-art option.\n\nProduction integrates the whole chain analytically for active time, offline time (up to one year) and Swarmwarp. Energy is capped and not produced during a warp. Backups export/import as JSON with a review before replacement. Lifetime journal persists across ascension. Original local single-player game: no online leaderboard or purchases. Quantities are bounded at 1e250 to keep long-term saves finite and portable. Respec refunds mutation investments but never category unlock costs.\n\nThree native .pvmod packages change meat, larvae or energy production and keep isolated saves. Store verifies package bytes, embeds all JavaScript offline, and source-checks/sanitizes career messages.\n')
p=r/'README.md';p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\nSwarm Sim preserves the classic idle insect growth structure with 20 meat tiers, 11 troop tiers, sacrifices, hatcheries, expansions, energy spells, cocoon storage, mutations and ascension. Original colony illustration, clear buy quantities/costs, analytic offline growth, backup import/export and three native mods. [Play Swarm Sim](./store/swarmsim/game.html).\n')
